      'RID rejections of major findings: make yourself available in Session 2; a rejected major RID must be confirmed by the reviewer or instructor. Credit a well-reasoned rejection as fully as an accepted fix, and refuse one that, like q12-12’s draft, rebuts a point the RID did not make.',
      'Teams with few RIDs received (late peer RIDs; lab plan L11 fallback) work from the instructor’s RIDs alone, as does a team whose own CP4 was late (Week 11 missing-CP4 rule); a team reviewed under the k+2 rule receives two peer RID sets and dispositions both.',
      'Graduate argument (optional this week): expect a clear intended use, one R64 method justified for it, a quantitative validation requirement and an honest partial-validation statement. Credit an argument that concludes the model is not yet credible enough and says what verdict VER-003 may return meanwhile.',
      'Accessibility: activities use labelled controls; the explorer shows the step bar as text (n/11) and the missing link in words; screens use ✓/✗/? with words, never colour alone.',
